# Build knobs for the arm64 benchmark. THIS FILE IS EDITABLE by the arm64
# optimization loop; .github/workflows/arm64-bench.yml, which consumes it, is
# not.
#
# That split exists so build-flag candidates (link-time optimization, target-cpu
# tuning) can be measured without editing the measuring instrument. A loop that
# may rewrite its own scoreboard is not measuring anything.
#
# Sourced by the workflow, so plain `KEY=value` only, no expansions. A value
# containing spaces MUST be quoted: `. file` parses `KEY=a b` as the assignment
# `KEY=a` followed by the command `b`, which exits 127 and fails the run instead
# of measuring anything (learned the direct way). The quotes are shell syntax
# and are consumed on sourcing, so they never reach the value.

# Cargo profile to build the benchmark and the gate with. `release` is what the
# shipped ARM artifacts currently use; `release-lto` (fat LTO, codegen-units=1)
# is defined in the root Cargo.toml but no ARM release has ever used it.
CARGO_PROFILE=release

# Extra RUSTFLAGS for the benchmark build. Empty = whatever the release build
# does today. Note -C target-cpu raises the artifact's ISA floor (stable rustc
# has no -Ctune-cpu), so anything set here must be scoped per-artifact before it
# ships, not applied globally.
BENCH_RUSTFLAGS=
